        "id": 1831528
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-13T18:38:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that the natural look up of this structure is by UUID, i.e. `HashMap\u003cUuid, ScannerInfo\u003e`.\n\nI agree that `HashMap\u003cCallbackId, Vec\u003cScannerInfo\u003e\u003e` would make disconnect much simpler, but it would make the simple Uuid lookup look a bit unnatural. The problem with unidiomatic \"remove and unregister all scanner having a specific callback id\" at disconnect will be solved by the Rust language when drain_filter is stable: https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.drain_filter.\n\nSince we expect that the number of scanners is low practically, I prefer to keep it simple this way. Also practically there will be very little CallbackId (maybe even 1 or 2, Chrome + Lacros) owning the ScannerInfos, so HashMapping by CallbackId provides little look up benefit. If you worry about performance, I prefer to change this to HashMap\u003cUuid, ScannerInfo\u003e since that will actually have the most look up performance benefit, while we can still solve the unidiomatic disconnect logic when drain_filter is in Rust stable.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "61a94208_270d94bd",
      "revId": "1664e0de76c765f8c61bbb87728ac811461e5fde",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
